  "evidencia": "Page: Centralia Massacre (Missouri). Sentence: The Centralia Massacre was an incident during the American Civil War in which twenty-four unarmed Union soldiers were captured and executed at Centralia, Missouri on September 27, 1864 by the pro-Confederate guerrilla leader William T. Anderson.\nPage: William T. Anderson. Sentence: William T. Anderson (1840 – October 26, 1864)—known as \"Bloody Bill\" Anderson—was one of the deadliest and most brutal pro-Confederate guerrilla leaders in the American Civil War.\nPage: Jesse James. Sentence: As followers of William Quantrill and \"Bloody Bill\" Anderson, they were accused of participating in atrocities against Union soldiers and civilian abolitionists, including the Centralia Massacre in 1864.\nPage: Huerfano County Courthouse and Jail. Sentence: The jail held Bob Ford, who killed Jesse James, and labor leader Mary \"Mother\" Jones.",
